  "_commit": {
    "id": "4663462124c3e5c2958ea6bbc231b8a6b05a32b3",
    "author": "theHumanBorch <ncborch@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "theHumanBorch <ncborch@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Remove evmix dependency\n\nCRAN is deprecating evmix, so the five GPD functions it supplied\n(dgpd, pgpd, qgpd, rgpd, fgpd) are now internal to\nclonalSizeDistribution(): .dgpd_internal, .pgpd_internal,\n.qgpd_internal, .rgpd_internal and .fgpd_internal. They reproduce\nevmix's numerical recipe exactly, including the abs(xi) < 1e-6 switch\nto the exponential limit, the strict x > u support test, and the\nGumbel moment-matched start values, so fitted models and the resulting\nJensen-Shannon distance matrices are unchanged.\n\nFitting the model also exposed three pre-existing defects:\n\n* .discgpdnll and .discgammanll raised an error when Nelder-Mead drove\n  the unconstrained log-scale parameter until exp() underflowed to\n  zero or overflowed. An optimizer exploring an invalid region needs\n  an infinite penalty it can step away from, not an exception that\n  discards the whole fit. Both now return Inf.\n\n* The GPD re-initialization in .fdiscgammagpd ran its quantile() and\n  .fgpd_internal() calls inside an error handler but outside the\n  tryCatch meant to contain them. A single excess above the threshold\n  left var() undefined, and the resulting NA escaped the handler and\n  killed the call.\n\n* which.min() on an all-NA vector returns integer(0), so a sample that\n  failed at every threshold died with \"attempt to select less than one\n  element in get1index\". clonalSizeDistribution() now explains the\n  cause and names the offending sample.\n\nVerified against devel across 36 cases at tolerance = 0: 32 identical\nor equally failing, 4 rescued (the 4- and 5-sample inputs, threshold =\n1:5 across all 8 samples, and the P20L fit), none broken, no changed\nvalues.\n\nA threshold that previously failed can now return a finite likelihood\nand win the grid search, so a multi-element `threshold` may select\ndifferently than it did in 2.9.4.\n\nBumps to 2.9.5. Adds tests pinning the internals to closed form rather\nthan to evmix.\n",
    "time": 1794851798
  },
